{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-23255","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23784","text":"PULSE v0.2 — Behavioral Loop Types"}]},{"id":"blk-23256","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23785","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-23786","text":" Design proposal (2026-05-27) — for review before implementation."}]},{"id":"blk-23257","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23787","marks":["bold"],"text":"Goal:"},{"id":"spn-23788","text":" Promote PULSE from a "},{"id":"spn-23789","marks":["italic"],"text":"structural schema"},{"id":"spn-23790","text":" (named phases + named tokens) to a "},{"id":"spn-23791","marks":["italic"],"text":"typed protocol"},{"id":"spn-23792","text":" (session-typed phases + linear tokens + projected choreography). Bring formal-spec quality to the level of behavioral type systems without losing the implementation maturity of v0.1.1."}]},{"id":"blk-23258","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23793","text":"Why"}]},{"id":"blk-23259","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23794","text":"PULSE v0.1.1 declares 5 phase kinds, 6 cross-loop tokens, and 7 invariants. The schema validates "},{"id":"spn-23795","marks":["italic"],"text":"names and shapes"},{"id":"spn-23796","text":" but cannot answer:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23261","spans":[{"id":"spn-23797","text":"Question v0.1.1 cannot answer"}]},{"id":"blk-23262","spans":[{"id":"spn-23798","text":"What's needed"}]}],"id":"blk-23260","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23263","spans":[{"id":"spn-23799","text":"Is this manifest deadlock-free?"}]},{"id":"blk-23264","spans":[{"id":"spn-23800","text":"Session-typed phase graph"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23265","spans":[{"id":"spn-23801","text":"Will every emitted "},{"id":"spn-23802","marks":["code"],"text":"SurpriseSignal"},{"id":"spn-23803","text":" be consumed?"}]},{"id":"blk-23266","spans":[{"id":"spn-23804","text":"Linear token typing"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23267","spans":[{"id":"spn-23805","text":"Is "},{"id":"spn-23806","marks":["code"],"text":"loop@v2"},{"id":"spn-23807","text":" a safe drop-in replacement for "},{"id":"spn-23808","marks":["code"],"text":"loop@v1"},{"id":"spn-23809","text":"?"}]},{"id":"blk-23268","spans":[{"id":"spn-23810","text":"Behavioral subtyping"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23269","spans":[{"id":"spn-23811","text":"If loop A sends X, will loop B receive a compatible X?"}]},{"id":"blk-23270","spans":[{"id":"spn-23812","text":"Multiparty choreography + projection"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23271","spans":[{"id":"spn-23813","text":"Does this phase's declared effect match its runtime behavior?"}]},{"id":"blk-23272","spans":[{"id":"spn-23814","text":"Effect rows + runtime fidelity check"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23273","spans":[{"id":"spn-23815","text":"Are the declared invariants actually true of this manifest?"}]},{"id":"blk-23274","spans":[{"id":"spn-23816","text":"Refinement-type checker"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23275","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23817","text":"Behavioral type systems (session types, multiparty session types, behavioral contracts) answer exactly these questions — but as preprints, not as running software. PULSE v0.2 ports the answers into a JSON-Schema-grounded substrate that already has 5 reference manifests and a conformance suite."}]},{"id":"blk-23276","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23818","text":"What it buys (scorecard delta)"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23278","spans":[{"id":"spn-23819","text":"Axis"}]},{"id":"blk-23279","spans":[{"id":"spn-23820","text":"v0.1.1"}]},{"id":"blk-23280","spans":[{"id":"spn-23821","text":"v0.2"}]},{"id":"blk-23281","spans":[{"id":"spn-23822","text":"Why"}]}],"id":"blk-23277","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23282","spans":[{"id":"spn-23823","text":"Formality"}]},{"id":"blk-23283","spans":[{"id":"spn-23824","text":"8"}]},{"id":"blk-23284","spans":[{"id":"spn-23825","marks":["bold"],"text":"10"}]},{"id":"blk-23285","spans":[{"id":"spn-23826","text":"Session-type-grade; refinement types on cadence/invariants; effect rows on phases"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23286","spans":[{"id":"spn-23827","text":"Compositionality"}]},{"id":"blk-23287","spans":[{"id":"spn-23828","text":"7"}]},{"id":"blk-23288","spans":[{"id":"spn-23829","marks":["bold"],"text":"10"}]},{"id":"blk-23289","spans":[{"id":"spn-23830","text":"Choreography + projection; linear tokens; behavioral subtyping"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23290","spans":[{"id":"spn-23831","text":"Substrate independence"}]},{"id":"blk-23291","spans":[{"id":"spn-23832","text":"9"}]},{"id":"blk-23292","spans":[{"id":"spn-23833","marks":["bold"],"text":"10"}]},{"id":"blk-23293","spans":[{"id":"spn-23834","text":"Typed protocol portable to any language with a type system"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23294","spans":[{"id":"spn-23835","text":"Closure"}]},{"id":"blk-23295","spans":[{"id":"spn-23836","text":"7"}]},{"id":"blk-23296","spans":[{"id":"spn-23837","marks":["bold"],"text":"9"}]},{"id":"blk-23297","spans":[{"id":"spn-23838","text":"Liveness + fidelity machine-checked; loses 1 for new verifier dependency"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23298","spans":[{"id":"spn-23839","marks":["bold"],"text":"Total / 40"}]},{"id":"blk-23299","spans":[{"id":"spn-23840","marks":["bold"],"text":"31"}]},{"id":"blk-23300","spans":[{"id":"spn-23841","marks":["bold"],"text":"39"}]},{"id":"blk-23301","spans":[{"id":"spn-23842","text":""}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23302","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23843","text":"For external context see "},{"id":"spn-23844","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/V0.2-BEHAVIORAL-TYPES-RATIONALE.md"},{"id":"spn-23845","text":" (planned) which compares this against Agent Behavioral Contracts (preprint), AgentRFC, and the CCS/CSP ceiling."}]},{"id":"blk-23303","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23846","text":"The six additions"}]},{"id":"blk-23304","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23847","text":"1. Typed token registry"}]},{"id":"blk-23305","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23848","marks":["bold"],"text":"File:"},{"id":"spn-23849","text":" "},{"id":"spn-23850","marks":["code"],"text":"schemas/pulse-tokens.v0.2.json"},{"id":"spn-23851","text":" (new)"}]},{"id":"blk-23306","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23852","text":"Each canonical token gets a payload schema, a linearity annotation, a variance annotation, and a TTL."}]},{"id":"blk-23307","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"tokens\": {\n    \"TopologyContext\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/topology_context.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"linear\",\n      \"variance\": \"covariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 60000,\n      \"description\": \"Emitted by retrieve, consumed by route. Loss would blind routing — must be consumed.\"\n    },\n    \"DeliberationRequest\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/deliberation_request.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"linear\",\n      \"variance\": \"invariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 300000,\n      \"description\": \"Triggers an inner deliberation loop. Loss would silently skip κ-resolution.\"\n    },\n    \"DeliberationResult\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/deliberation_result.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"linear\",\n      \"variance\": \"invariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 300000\n    },\n    \"OutcomeSignal\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/outcome_signal.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"linear\",\n      \"variance\": \"covariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 3600000,\n      \"description\": \"Audit primitive. Every action result must produce one — drop = audit failure.\"\n    },\n    \"ReputationUpdate\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/reputation_update.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"affine\",\n      \"variance\": \"covariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 86400000,\n      \"description\": \"Long-window aggregation; tolerates loss (drop down from linear because the next update overrides anyway).\"\n    },\n    \"ConsolidationEvent\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/consolidation_event.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"affine\",\n      \"variance\": \"covariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 3600000,\n      \"description\": \"Housekeeping signal; consolidate is idempotent.\"\n    },\n    \"SurpriseSignal\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/surprise_signal.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"linear\",\n      \"variance\": \"invariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 60000,\n      \"description\": \"OS-011 forward-model-prediction-error. Must be consumed.\"\n    },\n    \"SessionFidelityViolation\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/session_fidelity_violation.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"linear\",\n      \"variance\": \"invariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 86400000,\n      \"description\": \"Runtime-observed protocol violation. Must be reported, never silently dropped.\"\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-23308","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23853","marks":["bold"],"text":"Default for new canonical tokens: `linear`."},{"id":"spn-23854","text":" Authors must explicitly opt down to "},{"id":"spn-23855","marks":["code"],"text":"affine"},{"id":"spn-23856","text":" only when the token is observational, idempotent, or inherently lossy-tolerant (next emission overrides previous). This default flows from OS-010's \"every consequential signal must be audited\" thesis — silent loss is an audit failure; duplication is detected via idempotency keys at the substrate boundary."}]},{"id":"blk-23309","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23857","marks":["bold"],"text":"Linearity values:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23311","spans":[{"id":"spn-23858","text":"Value"}]},{"id":"blk-23312","spans":[{"id":"spn-23859","text":"Meaning"}]},{"id":"blk-23313","spans":[{"id":"spn-23860","text":"Checker enforces"}]}],"id":"blk-23310","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23314","spans":[{"id":"spn-23861","marks":["code"],"text":"linear"}]},{"id":"blk-23315","spans":[{"id":"spn-23862","text":"Exactly-once consumption"}]},{"id":"blk-23316","spans":[{"id":"spn-23863","text":"Emit ⇒ exactly one consumer; consumer is unique"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23317","spans":[{"id":"spn-23864","marks":["code"],"text":"affine"}]},{"id":"blk-23318","spans":[{"id":"spn-23865","text":"At-most-once consumption"}]},{"id":"blk-23319","spans":[{"id":"spn-23866","text":"Emit ⇒ at most one consumer (may drop)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23320","spans":[{"id":"spn-23867","marks":["code"],"text":"relevant"}]},{"id":"blk-23321","spans":[{"id":"spn-23868","text":"At-least-once consumption"}]},{"id":"blk-23322","spans":[{"id":"spn-23869","text":"Emit ⇒ at least one consumer (may duplicate)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23323","spans":[{"id":"spn-23870","marks":["code"],"text":"unrestricted"}]},{"id":"blk-23324","spans":[{"id":"spn-23871","text":"Any consumption"}]},{"id":"blk-23325","spans":[{"id":"spn-23872","text":"No constraint"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23326","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23873","marks":["bold"],"text":"Variance values:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23328","spans":[{"id":"spn-23874","text":"Value"}]},{"id":"blk-23329","spans":[{"id":"spn-23875","text":"Meaning"}]}],"id":"blk-23327","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23330","spans":[{"id":"spn-23876","marks":["code"],"text":"covariant"}]},{"id":"blk-23331","spans":[{"id":"spn-23877","text":"Subtype payloads acceptable on the consumer side"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23332","spans":[{"id":"spn-23878","marks":["code"],"text":"contravariant"}]},{"id":"blk-23333","spans":[{"id":"spn-23879","text":"Supertype payloads acceptable on the producer side"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23334","spans":[{"id":"spn-23880","marks":["code"],"text":"invariant"}]},{"id":"blk-23335","spans":[{"id":"spn-23881","text":"Exact payload schema match required"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23336","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23882","marks":["bold"],"text":"Required payload schemas:"},{"id":"spn-23883","text":" Each token gets its own JSON Schema under "},{"id":"spn-23884","marks":["code"],"text":"schemas/tokens/"},{"id":"spn-23885","text":". "},{"id":"spn-23886","marks":["bold"],"text":"Eight"},{"id":"spn-23887","text":" new schema files (the six v0.1.1 canonical tokens + two added in v0.2: "},{"id":"spn-23888","marks":["code"],"text":"DeliberationRequest"},{"id":"spn-23889","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23890","marks":["code"],"text":"SessionFidelityViolation"},{"id":"spn-23891","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-23337","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23892","text":"Token evolution rules (registry-level subtyping only)"}]},{"id":"blk-23338","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23893","text":"Token payload evolution happens "},{"id":"spn-23894","marks":["bold"],"text":"in the global registry, never per-loop"},{"id":"spn-23895","text":". This flows from OS-010 §1019–1051 (\"canonical tokens stable through v1.0; additive-only without minor bump; vendor-namespacing for custom tokens\")."}]},{"id":"blk-23339","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23341","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23896","marks":["bold"],"text":"Additive-only within a minor version."},{"id":"spn-23897","text":" Adding optional fields to a"}]}],"id":"blk-23340","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-23342","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23898","text":"token's payload schema is allowed without bumping the token's version. Removing or renaming fields requires a minor version bump and 12-month notice (per OS-010 stability policy)."}]},{"id":"blk-23343","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23345","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23899","marks":["bold"],"text":"Registry tracks the partial order."},{"id":"spn-23900","text":" The registry asserts"}]}],"id":"blk-23344","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-23346","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23901","marks":["code"],"text":"topology_context.v0.2 <: topology_context.v0.1"},{"id":"spn-23902","text":" when the v0.2 schema is an additive extension of v0.1. The behavioral subtyping checker (§5) consults the registry rather than re-deriving compatibility."}]},{"id":"blk-23347","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23349","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23903","marks":["bold"],"text":"No per-loop token variants."},{"id":"spn-23904","text":" A loop that needs a custom payload"}]}],"id":"blk-23348","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-23350","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23905","text":"must register a vendor-namespaced token (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-23906","marks":["code"],"text":"acme.v1.AcmeOutcome"},{"id":"spn-23907","text":") in the registry and reference it canonically from its manifest. Loops never declare local subtypes of canonical tokens — that would explode the cross-loop vocabulary and break PRISM's ability to benchmark heterogeneous systems against a shared evaluation grammar."}]},{"id":"blk-23351","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23908","text":"2. Phase signatures with effect rows"}]},{"id":"blk-23352","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23909","marks":["bold"],"text":"Change:"},{"id":"spn-23910","text":" Extend the existing "},{"id":"spn-23911","marks":["code"],"text":"phases[]"},{"id":"spn-23912","text":" entries in "},{"id":"spn-23913","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.2.json"},{"id":"spn-23914","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-23915","marks":["code"],"text":"inputs"},{"id":"spn-23916","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23917","marks":["code"],"text":"outputs"},{"id":"spn-23918","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23919","marks":["code"],"text":"effects"},{"id":"spn-23920","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23921","marks":["code"],"text":"successors"},{"id":"spn-23922","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-23923","marks":["code"],"text":"refinements"},{"id":"spn-23924","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-23353","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"retrieve_context\",\n      \"kind\": \"retrieve\",\n      \"inputs\":  { \"tokens\": [], \"substrates\": [\"memory\"] },\n      \"outputs\": { \"tokens\": [\"TopologyContext\"] },\n      \"effects\": {\n        \"calls\":    [\"memory.retrieve_context\", \"memory.topology_analyze\"],\n        \"mutates\":  [],\n        \"may_emit\": [],\n        \"external\": []\n      },\n      \"successors\": [\"route_topology\"],\n      \"refinements\": {\n        \"latency_ms_max\": 200,\n        \"deterministic\": false\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"route_topology\",\n      \"kind\": \"route\",\n      \"inputs\":  { \"tokens\": [\"TopologyContext\"], \"substrates\": [] },\n      \"outputs\": { \"tokens\": [] },\n      \"effects\": {\n        \"calls\":    [],\n        \"mutates\":  [],\n        \"may_emit\": [\"DeliberationRequest\"],\n        \"external\": []\n      },\n      \"successors\": [\"deliberate\", \"act_node_write\"],\n      \"refinements\": {\n        \"branch_predicate\": \"topology.routing\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-23354","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23925","marks":["bold"],"text":"Effect row fields:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23356","spans":[{"id":"spn-23926","text":"Field"}]},{"id":"blk-23357","spans":[{"id":"spn-23927","text":"What it tracks"}]}],"id":"blk-23355","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23358","spans":[{"id":"spn-23928","marks":["code"],"text":"calls"}]},{"id":"blk-23359","spans":[{"id":"spn-23929","text":"Substrate operation IDs invoked (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-23930","marks":["code"],"text":"memory.retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-23931","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23932","marks":["code"],"text":"policy.check_policy"},{"id":"spn-23933","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23360","spans":[{"id":"spn-23934","marks":["code"],"text":"mutates"}]},{"id":"blk-23361","spans":[{"id":"spn-23935","text":"Substrate operation IDs that change state (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-23936","marks":["code"],"text":"memory.store_node"},{"id":"spn-23937","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23938","marks":["code"],"text":"audit.append_event"},{"id":"spn-23939","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23362","spans":[{"id":"spn-23940","marks":["code"],"text":"may_emit"}]},{"id":"blk-23363","spans":[{"id":"spn-23941","text":"Token names this phase may produce"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23364","spans":[{"id":"spn-23942","marks":["code"],"text":"external"}]},{"id":"blk-23365","spans":[{"id":"spn-23943","text":"External resources touched (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-23944","marks":["code"],"text":"http://*"},{"id":"spn-23945","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23946","marks":["code"],"text":"mcp://prism"},{"id":"spn-23947","text":")"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23366","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23948","marks":["bold"],"text":"Granularity is operation-level, not storage-level."},{"id":"spn-23949","text":" Effect rows reference the substrate API surface defined in OS-010 §9 (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-23950","marks":["code"],"text":"memory.retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-23951","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23952","marks":["code"],"text":"audit.append_event"},{"id":"spn-23953","text":"), never specific storage paths like "},{"id":"spn-23954","marks":["code"],"text":"sqlite.kg.nodes"},{"id":"spn-23955","text":". This flows from the \"substrate independence\" thesis: the spec must not assume a relational backend, and graphonomous swapping SQLite for Postgres should not require manifest changes."}]},{"id":"blk-23367","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23956","marks":["bold"],"text":"Refinement values:"},{"id":"spn-23957","text":" key-value predicates. A small vendored evaluator handles the supported subset; unknown keys are passed through as documentation."}]},{"id":"blk-23368","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23958","marks":["bold"],"text":"Supported refinement predicates (vendored mini-evaluator):"}]},{"id":"blk-23369","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23371","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23959","text":"Comparison: "},{"id":"spn-23960","marks":["code"],"text":"≤"},{"id":"spn-23961","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23962","marks":["code"],"text":"<"},{"id":"spn-23963","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23964","marks":["code"],"text":"≥"},{"id":"spn-23965","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23966","marks":["code"],"text":">"},{"id":"spn-23967","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23968","marks":["code"],"text":"=="},{"id":"spn-23969","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23970","marks":["code"],"text":"!="},{"id":"spn-23971","text":" on numeric or string literals"}]}],"id":"blk-23370","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23373","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23972","text":"Boolean conjunction ("},{"id":"spn-23973","marks":["code"],"text":"∧"},{"id":"spn-23974","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-23975","marks":["code"],"text":"&&"},{"id":"spn-23976","text":") and disjunction ("},{"id":"spn-23977","marks":["code"],"text":"∨"},{"id":"spn-23978","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-23979","marks":["code"],"text":"||"},{"id":"spn-23980","text":") over the above"}]}],"id":"blk-23372","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23375","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23981","text":"Set membership: "},{"id":"spn-23982","marks":["code"],"text":"value in [a, b, c]"}]}],"id":"blk-23374","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23377","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23983","text":"Negation of any of the above"}]}],"id":"blk-23376","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-23378","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23984","text":"No Z3, no external SMT solver, no optional peer dependency. The vendored evaluator is a few hundred lines of TypeScript in "},{"id":"spn-23985","marks":["code"],"text":"src/refinement.ts"},{"id":"spn-23986","text":" and runs in any environment that runs npm. The ≤25KB processor target from STACK_ARCHITECTURE_GAP_REVIEW.md applies here too."}]},{"id":"blk-23379","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23987","text":"Recognized refinement keys in v0.2:"}]},{"id":"blk-23380","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23382","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23988","marks":["code"],"text":"latency_ms_max"},{"id":"spn-23989","text":" (number) — checker emits a benchmark assertion"}]}],"id":"blk-23381","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23384","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23990","marks":["code"],"text":"deterministic"},{"id":"spn-23991","text":" (boolean) — flagged in conformance T-DET"}]}],"id":"blk-23383","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23386","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23992","marks":["code"],"text":"branch_predicate"},{"id":"spn-23993","text":" (string) — referenced expression must appear in a"}]}],"id":"blk-23385","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-23387","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23994","text":"consumed token's payload schema"}]},{"id":"blk-23388","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23390","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23995","marks":["code"],"text":"idempotent"},{"id":"spn-23996","text":" (boolean) — extends existing T03 phase-idempotency check"}]}],"id":"blk-23389","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23392","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23997","marks":["code"],"text":"requires_kappa"},{"id":"spn-23998","text":" (string, e.g. "},{"id":"spn-23999","marks":["code"],"text":"\"== 0\""},{"id":"spn-24000","text":", "},{"id":"spn-24001","marks":["code"],"text":"\"> 0\""},{"id":"spn-24002","text":") — routing precondition"}]}],"id":"blk-23391","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-23393","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24003","text":"3. Local session type (derived, validated)"}]},{"id":"blk-23394","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24004","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not stored in the manifest"},{"id":"spn-24005","text":" — derived by the checker from the phase graph. Expressed internally as a regular expression over phase IDs (or an equivalent finite automaton)."}]},{"id":"blk-23395","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24006","text":"For graphonomous.continual_learning the derived session type is:"}]},{"id":"blk-23396","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"loop = retrieve_context · route_topology\n     · ( deliberate · act_node_write\n       | act_node_write )\n     · learn_outcome\n     · ( consolidate )?"},{"id":"blk-23397","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24007","marks":["bold"],"text":"Checker proves:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23399","spans":[{"id":"spn-24008","text":"Property"}]},{"id":"blk-23400","spans":[{"id":"spn-24009","text":"How"}]}],"id":"blk-23398","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23401","spans":[{"id":"spn-24010","marks":["bold"],"text":"Reachability"}]},{"id":"blk-23402","spans":[{"id":"spn-24011","text":"Every declared phase is reachable from an entry phase"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23403","spans":[{"id":"spn-24012","marks":["bold"],"text":"Progress"}]},{"id":"blk-23404","spans":[{"id":"spn-24013","text":"From any reachable phase a successor exists, or the loop terminates explicitly"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23405","spans":[{"id":"spn-24014","marks":["bold"],"text":"No deadlock"}]},{"id":"blk-23406","spans":[{"id":"spn-24015","text":"The successor relation has no cycles that can't make progress"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23407","spans":[{"id":"spn-24016","marks":["bold"],"text":"Token discipline"}]},{"id":"blk-23408","spans":[{"id":"spn-24017","text":"Every linear token emit has exactly one matching consumer reachable downstream; every affine has at most one"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23409","spans":[{"id":"spn-24018","marks":["bold"],"text":"Effect monotonicity"}]},{"id":"blk-23410","spans":[{"id":"spn-24019","text":"A phase's declared effect row is a superset of its successors' assumed reads"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23411","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24020","text":"Output of "},{"id":"spn-24021","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse check <manifest>"},{"id":"spn-24022","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-23412","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"✓ session type derives: retrieve · route · (deliberate? · act) · learn · consolidate?\n✓ all 8 canonical token consumers resolved\n✓ all linear tokens have unique consumers\n✓ all 7 invariants hold under refinement (vendored evaluator)\n✓ progress: from any reachable phase, a successor exists\n✓ liveness: retrieve is reachable from all phases"},{"id":"blk-23413","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24023","text":"4. Global choreography + projection"}]},{"id":"blk-23414","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24024","marks":["bold"],"text":"Schema:"},{"id":"spn-24025","text":" "},{"id":"spn-24026","marks":["code"],"text":"schemas/pulse-choreography.v0.2.json"},{"id":"spn-24027","text":" (new) "},{"id":"spn-24028","marks":["bold"],"text":"File pattern:"},{"id":"spn-24029","text":" "},{"id":"spn-24030","marks":["code"],"text":"manifests/<name>.choreography.json"}]},{"id":"blk-23415","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24031","text":"Choreographies live "},{"id":"spn-24032","marks":["bold"],"text":"alongside loop manifests in `manifests/`"},{"id":"spn-24033","text":", not in a separate top-level directory. This flows from the \"Topology as Authority\" thesis: a choreography is a higher-arity topology declaration (3+ participants) but still the same kind of artifact. Co-location keeps the authority for cross-loop topology in one place. No new "},{"id":"spn-24034","marks":["code"],"text":"choreographies/"},{"id":"spn-24035","text":" directory is created."}]},{"id":"blk-23416","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24036","text":"Currently each manifest is local. v0.2 adds an optional "},{"id":"spn-24037","marks":["bold"],"text":"global type"},{"id":"spn-24038","text":" that describes the cross-loop dance and projects to per-loop connection blocks."}]},{"id":"blk-23417","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://opensentience.org/schemas/pulse-choreography.v0.2.json\",\n  \"choreography_id\": \"ecosystem.continual_learning_with_prism\",\n  \"version\": \"0.2.0\",\n  \"participants\": [\n    \"graphonomous.continual_learning\",\n    \"prism.benchmark\",\n    \"agentromatic.deliberation\"\n  ],\n  \"global_type\": [\n    {\n      \"step\": 1,\n      \"from\": \"graphonomous.continual_learning\",\n      \"to\":   \"agentromatic.deliberation\",\n      \"token\": \"DeliberationRequest\",\n      \"guard\": \"topology.kappa > 0\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"step\": 2,\n      \"from\": \"agentromatic.deliberation\",\n      \"to\":   \"graphonomous.continual_learning\",\n      \"token\": \"DeliberationResult\",\n      \"after\": [1]\n    },\n    {\n      \"step\": 3,\n      \"from\": \"graphonomous.continual_learning\",\n      \"to\":   \"prism.benchmark\",\n      \"token\": \"OutcomeSignal\",\n      \"cadence\": \"per_action\",\n      \"after\":  [2]\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-23418","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24039","marks":["bold"],"text":"Projection algorithm."},{"id":"spn-24040","text":" Given a choreography C and participant P, produce the local view C↓P — a sequence of \"emit X\" / \"expect X\" obligations that the participant's PULSE manifest must satisfy. The checker then verifies each participant's "},{"id":"spn-24041","marks":["code"],"text":"connections"},{"id":"spn-24042","text":" block is consistent with its projection."}]},{"id":"blk-23419","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24043","marks":["bold"],"text":"Soundness theorem (informal, follows MPST canon):"},{"id":"spn-24044","text":" If every participant locally type-checks against its projection, the choreography is "},{"id":"spn-24045","marks":["italic"],"text":"deadlock-free, communication-safe, and progresses to termination"},{"id":"spn-24046","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-23420","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24047","text":"A choreography can declare nesting (sub-choreographies) and parallel branches ("},{"id":"spn-24048","marks":["code"],"text":"parallel: [step_a, step_b]"},{"id":"spn-24049","text":") using existing PULSE primitives."}]},{"id":"blk-23421","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24050","text":"5. Behavioral subtyping for version compatibility"}]},{"id":"blk-23422","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24051","marks":["bold"],"text":"New CLI:"},{"id":"spn-24052","text":" "},{"id":"spn-24053","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse compat <loop_a@v> <loop_b@v>"}]},{"id":"blk-23423","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24054","text":"Replaces the de-facto policy of \"bump the version and pray\" with a machine-checked subtyping relation:"}]},{"id":"blk-23424","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"A <: B iff\n  phases:        A.phases ⊇ B.phases                       (extension allowed)\n  inputs:        ∀ p ∈ B: p_A.inputs    ⊆ p_B.inputs        (contravariant)\n  outputs:       ∀ p ∈ B: p_A.outputs   ⊇ p_B.outputs       (covariant)\n  effects:       ∀ p ∈ B: p_A.effects   ⊆ p_B.effects       (subeffecting)\n  linearity:     A.linear_tokens ⊇ B.linear_tokens          (no relaxation)\n  invariants:    A.invariants ⊇ B.invariants                (only added, not dropped)\n  cadence:       A.cadence refines B.cadence                (tighter, not looser)"},{"id":"blk-23425","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24055","text":"Output:"}]},{"id":"blk-23426","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"$ pulse compat graphonomous.continual_learning@0.4.3 \\\n              graphonomous.continual_learning@0.4.4\n\n✓ phases: superset (added: episodic_replay)\n✓ inputs: contravariant (no widenings broken)\n✓ outputs: covariant\n✓ effects: subeffecting holds\n✓ linearity: SurpriseSignal added as linear (additive)\n✓ invariants: superset (added: I7-episodic-monotonic)\n✓ cadence: unchanged\n\nVERDICT: 0.4.4 IS a safe behavioral subtype of 0.4.3."},{"id":"blk-23427","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24056","text":"Failed-compat verdict includes a counterexample trace."}]},{"id":"blk-23428","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24057","text":"6. Conformance checker (offline + runtime)"}]},{"id":"blk-23429","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24058","marks":["bold"],"text":"Existing:"},{"id":"spn-24059","text":" "},{"id":"spn-24060","marks":["code"],"text":"src/conformance.ts"},{"id":"spn-24061","text":" already runs the 12 v0.1 tests. v0.2 adds:"}]},{"id":"blk-23430","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24062","marks":["bold"],"text":"Offline checks (new):"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23432","spans":[{"id":"spn-24063","text":"ID"}]},{"id":"blk-23433","spans":[{"id":"spn-24064","text":"Test"}]}],"id":"blk-23431","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23434","spans":[{"id":"spn-24065","text":"T13"}]},{"id":"blk-23435","spans":[{"id":"spn-24066","text":"Session-type derivation succeeds"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23436","spans":[{"id":"spn-24067","text":"T14"}]},{"id":"blk-23437","spans":[{"id":"spn-24068","text":"Reachability of all declared phases"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23438","spans":[{"id":"spn-24069","text":"T15"}]},{"id":"blk-23439","spans":[{"id":"spn-24070","text":"Progress (no stuck states)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23440","spans":[{"id":"spn-24071","text":"T16"}]},{"id":"blk-23441","spans":[{"id":"spn-24072","text":"Linear-token consumer uniqueness"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23442","spans":[{"id":"spn-24073","text":"T17"}]},{"id":"blk-23443","spans":[{"id":"spn-24074","text":"Affine-token consumer cap"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23444","spans":[{"id":"spn-24075","text":"T18"}]},{"id":"blk-23445","spans":[{"id":"spn-24076","text":"Effect row monotonicity"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23446","spans":[{"id":"spn-24077","text":"T19"}]},{"id":"blk-23447","spans":[{"id":"spn-24078","text":"Refinement satisfiability (vendored mini-evaluator)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23448","spans":[{"id":"spn-24079","text":"T20"}]},{"id":"blk-23449","spans":[{"id":"spn-24080","text":"Choreography projection consistency (if member)"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23450","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24081","marks":["bold"],"text":"Runtime checks (new):"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23452","spans":[{"id":"spn-24082","text":"ID"}]},{"id":"blk-23453","spans":[{"id":"spn-24083","text":"Test"}]}],"id":"blk-23451","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23454","spans":[{"id":"spn-24084","text":"T21"}]},{"id":"blk-23455","spans":[{"id":"spn-24085","text":"Session fidelity — observed phase trace matches derived session type"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23456","spans":[{"id":"spn-24086","text":"T22"}]},{"id":"blk-23457","spans":[{"id":"spn-24087","text":"Linear-token actually-consumed-once (over trace window)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23458","spans":[{"id":"spn-24088","text":"T23"}]},{"id":"blk-23459","spans":[{"id":"spn-24089","text":"Effect-row honesty — observed substrate calls ⊆ declared "},{"id":"spn-24090","marks":["code"],"text":"calls"},{"id":"spn-24091","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-24092","marks":["code"],"text":"mutates"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23460","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24093","text":"On violation the checker emits a new canonical token, "},{"id":"spn-24094","marks":["code"],"text":"SessionFidelityViolation"},{"id":"spn-24095","text":", itself PULSE-typed, so violations flow through the same envelope plumbing as other signals."}]},{"id":"blk-23461","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24096","text":"Token canon update"}]},{"id":"blk-23462","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24097","text":"v0.2 adds two tokens to the canonical set:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23464","spans":[{"id":"spn-24098","text":"Token"}]},{"id":"blk-23465","spans":[{"id":"spn-24099","text":"Phase emitter"}]},{"id":"blk-23466","spans":[{"id":"spn-24100","text":"Linearity"}]},{"id":"blk-23467","spans":[{"id":"spn-24101","text":"Purpose"}]}],"id":"blk-23463","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23468","spans":[{"id":"spn-24102","marks":["code"],"text":"DeliberationRequest"}]},{"id":"blk-23469","spans":[{"id":"spn-24103","marks":["code"],"text":"route"}]},{"id":"blk-23470","spans":[{"id":"spn-24104","text":"linear"}]},{"id":"blk-23471","spans":[{"id":"spn-24105","text":"Triggers an inner deliberation loop (split out of overloaded routing)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23472","spans":[{"id":"spn-24106","marks":["code"],"text":"SessionFidelityViolation"}]},{"id":"blk-23473","spans":[{"id":"spn-24107","text":"conformance runtime"}]},{"id":"blk-23474","spans":[{"id":"spn-24108","text":"linear"}]},{"id":"blk-23475","spans":[{"id":"spn-24109","text":"Reports a runtime-observed protocol violation"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23476","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24110","text":"Total canonical tokens in v0.2: "},{"id":"spn-24111","marks":["bold"],"text":"8"},{"id":"spn-24112","text":" (was 6 in v0.1.1)."}]},{"id":"blk-23477","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24113","text":"Backwards compatibility"}]},{"id":"blk-23478","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24114","text":"v0.1.1 manifests "},{"id":"spn-24115","marks":["bold"],"text":"continue to validate"},{"id":"spn-24116","text":" under v0.2 — every new field is optional. A v0.1.1 manifest validated under v0.2 schema receives:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23480","spans":[{"id":"spn-24117","text":"Field"}]},{"id":"blk-23481","spans":[{"id":"spn-24118","text":"Default when absent"}]}],"id":"blk-23479","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23482","spans":[{"id":"spn-24119","marks":["code"],"text":"phases[].inputs"}]},{"id":"blk-23483","spans":[{"id":"spn-24120","marks":["code"],"text":"{ \"tokens\": [], \"substrates\": [] }"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23484","spans":[{"id":"spn-24121","marks":["code"],"text":"phases[].outputs"}]},{"id":"blk-23485","spans":[{"id":"spn-24122","marks":["code"],"text":"{ \"tokens\": [] }"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23486","spans":[{"id":"spn-24123","marks":["code"],"text":"phases[].effects"}]},{"id":"blk-23487","spans":[{"id":"spn-24124","marks":["code"],"text":"{ \"calls\": [], \"mutates\": [], \"may_emit\": [], \"external\": [] }"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23488","spans":[{"id":"spn-24125","marks":["code"],"text":"phases[].refinements"}]},{"id":"blk-23489","spans":[{"id":"spn-24126","marks":["code"],"text":"{}"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23490","spans":[{"id":"spn-24127","text":"Token registry lookups"}]},{"id":"blk-23491","spans":[{"id":"spn-24128","text":"Falls back to v0.1.1 implicit semantics (linear by default for canonical tokens, invariant, TTL = ∞)"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23492","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24129","text":"The checker reports v0.1.1-default manifests with "},{"id":"spn-24130","marks":["code"],"text":"degraded_checks: true"},{"id":"spn-24131","text":" — they pass T01–T12 but cannot pass T13–T23. Owners are nudged to enrich."}]},{"id":"blk-23493","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24132","text":"Non-goals"}]},{"id":"blk-23494","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23496","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24133","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not"},{"id":"spn-24134","text":" a process-algebra spec. PULSE v0.2 is session-typed, not"}]}],"id":"blk-23495","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-23497","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24135","text":"CCS/CSP-modeled. Process-algebra-grade deadlock-freedom across parallel sub-agents is a future v0.3 question."}]},{"id":"blk-23498","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23500","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24136","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not"},{"id":"spn-24137","text":" an SMT/Z3 dependency. The refinement checker is a vendored"}]}],"id":"blk-23499","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-23501","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24138","text":"mini-evaluator over ≤/≥/==/membership/conjunction/disjunction. Z3 is neither a runtime dependency nor an optional peer dep. If a complex constraint can't be evaluated locally, the checker emits a warning and runtime fidelity (T21–T23) catches violations."}]},{"id":"blk-23502","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23504","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24139","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not"},{"id":"spn-24140","text":" an MPST formalization paper. v0.2 follows MPST principles but"}]}],"id":"blk-23503","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-23505","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24141","text":"targets working software, not formal verification literature."}]},{"id":"blk-23506","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24142","text":"Resolved design questions (closed 2026-05-27)"}]},{"id":"blk-23507","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24143","text":"All five open questions are resolved against the project's stated thesis (see "},{"id":"spn-24144","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/V0.2-RATIONALE.md"},{"id":"spn-24145","text":" for the per-question evidence trail across OS-010, STACK_ARCHITECTURE_GAP_REVIEW.md, STACK_PLANNING.md, and the prompt set)."}]},{"id":"blk-23508","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23510","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24146","marks":["bold"],"text":"Linearity default."},{"id":"spn-24147","text":" "},{"id":"spn-24148","marks":["bold"],"text":"Resolved: `linear`"},{"id":"spn-24149","text":" for new canonical tokens."}]}],"id":"blk-23509","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-23511","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24150","text":"Authors opt down to "},{"id":"spn-24151","marks":["code"],"text":"affine"},{"id":"spn-24152","text":" only for observational/idempotent/lossy- tolerant tokens. Flows from OS-010 §7.3 + §10.2 (\"fail loud, leave a trace; silent loss is an audit failure\")."}]},{"id":"blk-23512","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23514","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24153","marks":["bold"],"text":"Choreography artifact location."},{"id":"spn-24154","text":" **Resolved: co-located in"}]}],"id":"blk-23513","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-23515","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24155","marks":["code"],"text":"manifests/"},{"id":"spn-24156","text":".** No new top-level directory. Flows from STACK_TOPOLOGY_AS_AUTHORITY thesis — a choreography is a higher-arity topology artifact, same kind as a loop manifest."}]},{"id":"blk-23516","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23518","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24157","marks":["bold"],"text":"Effect row granularity."},{"id":"spn-24158","text":" **Resolved: operation-level, not"}]}],"id":"blk-23517","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-23519","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24159","text":"storage-level.** Effect rows reference substrate API operations from OS-010 §9 (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-24160","marks":["code"],"text":"memory.retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-24161","text":"), never storage paths. Flows from \"substrate independence\" (OS-010 §3.4) and the \"falsifiable processor\" gate (STACK_ARCHITECTURE_GAP_REVIEW Finding 1)."}]},{"id":"blk-23520","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23522","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24162","marks":["bold"],"text":"Refinement checker dependency."},{"id":"spn-24163","text":" **Resolved: vendor a tiny"}]}],"id":"blk-23521","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-23523","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24164","text":"evaluator.** No Z3, no SMT, no optional peer dep. Covers ≤/≥/==/ membership/∧/∨/¬. Flows from \"tiny core, max portability\" and the ≤25KB processor target (STACK_ARCHITECTURE_GAP_REVIEW Finding 2)."}]},{"id":"blk-23524","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23526","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24165","marks":["bold"],"text":"Per-loop token subtyping."},{"id":"spn-24166","text":" "},{"id":"spn-24167","marks":["bold"],"text":"Resolved: prohibited."},{"id":"spn-24168","text":" Token payload"}]}],"id":"blk-23525","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":5},{"id":"blk-23527","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24169","text":"evolution happens only in the global registry, by additive-only rules. Custom payloads must vendor-namespace (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-24170","marks":["code"],"text":"acme.v1.X"},{"id":"spn-24171","text":"). Flows from OS-010 §1019–1051 (ecosystem-wide vocabulary stability) and STACK_PLANNING.md vendor-namespace pattern."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieradujh54w7hk3v47kq4sbfeijarczw2aitpgkpdqaqf7oolkh7tjjq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}